.TH IAD\-META\-PARENT\-COMPONENT 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
meta_parent_component \- See the module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
MetaParentComponent::new(registry: &'a Registry<Id, K>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBMetaParentComponent\fR: a container that \fBnotifies its meta children\fR to switch between their modes. It owns no content of its own and no state; the app owns a \fBMetaRegistry\fR and the parent reads it.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRegistration.\fR Every child registers separately and announces the actions it implements: \fBregister\fR takes them from a \fBMetaComponent\fR (the keys its variants are selected by), and \fBRegistry::register\fR takes them from any component that has modes of its own, such as a \fBReorderableList\fR (\fBMode::Edit\fR and \fBMode::Preview\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNotification.\fR \fBregistry.notify(&action)\fR switches exactly the children that announced \fBaction\fR. A child that did not announce it (an *unrelated* \fBMetaComponent\fR) and a child that never registered (any non\-meta widget) are left as they are.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDisplay.\fR \fBmeta\fR puts a registered \fBMetaComponent\fR in with the action it was last switched to as its selection; \fBlistener\fR hands that action to a closure that builds any other mode\-aware component; \fBchild\fR adds a plain element that is never notified.
.PP
.nf
.RS
// once, when the app starts: each child announces what it implements
let mut modes = Registry::new();
MetaParentComponent::register(&mut modes, "bar", &search_bar());        // Bar::Search...
modes.register("list", [Mode::Edit, Mode::Preview]);                     // a ReorderableList

// in update: tell the children
modes.notify(&Mode::Edit);                    // "list" switches; "bar" does not

// in view
MetaParentComponent::new(&modes)
    .meta("bar", search_bar())                // switched, if it announced the action
    .on_child_event(Msg::Child)               // what children report: (id, ChildEvent)
    .listener("list", |mode, report| {
        ReorderableList::of(&self.order, row)
            .editing(mode == Some(&Mode::Edit))
            .on_event(Msg::List)              // the list's own message
            .on_change(report.on_change())    // and the parent's, independently
            .into()
    })
    .child(title_text)                        // never notified
.RE
.fi
