A registered child that is not a \fBMetaComponent\fR but has modes of its own: \fBbuild\fR gets the action it was last switched to (\fBNone\fR before any).
.PP
It also gets a \fBReporter\fR to wire the child's own events to the parent's \fBon_child_event\fR callback.
.TP
.B \&.child(child: impl Into<Element<'a, M>>)
A plain child. It does not register and is never notified.
.SH EVENTS
Callbacks that produce the application's message.
.TP
.B \&.on_child_event(f: impl Fn(Id, ChildEvent) \-> M + 'a)
The parent's own callback for what its children report (a list's order changing): it gets the child's id and the \fBChildEvent\fR. Set it *before* the listeners that report. Independent of the callbacks the children carry themselves; the app can run \fBRegistry::emit\fR on it and react, e.g. by notifying other children.
